<title>NORWAY: Statoil delays Barents Sea well.</title>
<headline>Statoil delays Barents Sea well.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) said on Thursday it had postponed indefinitely an exploration well planned in the North Cape Basin of the Barents Sea because of a delay with the rig Transocean Arctic.</p>
<p>The rig had been working for Saga Petroleum ASA on production licence 199 off mid-Norway. Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said the delay meant it would not be able to complete work before the summer ban on Barents Sea drilling.</p>
<p>Transocean Arctic was originally due to drill two wells in northern waters for Statoil and Saga respectively. It will now go directly to the Aasgard development in the Norwegian Sea for production drilling.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +_47 22 42 50 41</p>
